- Direct assessment of bowel pattern (stool frequency/consistency *per week*, presence of large/hard stools, soiling, abdominal distension, or retentive behaviors);  
- Growth parameters (weight/length), which are essential to rule out failure to thrive — a red flag for systemic or organic disease;  
- Developmental screening data — irritability may be an early behavioral marker of autism spectrum disorder, language delay, or hearing impairment (e.g., undiagnosed otitis media or sensorineural loss);  
- CBC result — still pending/unconfirmed; iron deficiency anemia remains plausible given age and irritability, and would be treatable and consequential if missed;  
